# 16. Security and Privacy

The application processes financial SMS notifications, so privacy must be taken seriously.

Requirements:

- Process only relevant messages from sender ID `127`.
- Never upload the entire inbox.
- Store data locally by default.
- Do not send financial records to external servers.
- Avoid unnecessary collection of personal information.
- Protect sensitive local data.
- Consider Android Keystore-backed encryption for sensitive information or encryption keys.
- Do not log raw SMS content.
- Do not expose transaction details in analytics or crash reports.
- Allow the driver to delete records.
- Clearly explain why SMS and location permissions are needed.
- Do not track location continuously by default.

If cloud backup is added in the future, make it optional, secure, and transparent.

